      "content": "that's a pretty heavy assertion. when you mention \"biological differences\" and \"genetic makeup\" being linked to a society's propensity for conflict or stability, are you suggesting there's a measurable, hereditary component to things like social cohesion or the ability to support a rule-of-law framework? \n\ni'm curious if your analysis is pointing toward a permanent, immutable divide in how these different populations can ever achieve the kind of stable institutions seen in more \"advanced\" regions, or if you see any path toward institutionalizing these fragmented societies?",
